# MotionField local patch — ComfyUI-MuseTalk for Apple Silicon / ComfyUI 0.41 / py3.14
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/chaojie/ComfyUI-MuseTalk  (MIT License)
# Pinned commit: 84f4b6dcbb0d87e87687f324092056646582457d ("fix bugs", 2024-04-05)
#
# Apply with:  git apply scripts/patches/comfyui-musetalk-mps.patch
# Reproduce:   scripts/setup-musetalk.sh <comfyui-dir>
#
# What it changes:
#  - nodes.py: lazy ~4 GB weight load (upstream loads at import), CUDA->MPS/CPU
#    device pick, optional AUDIO-tensor input for MuseTalkRun (LoadAudio/TTS
#    graphs feed it directly), uploaded-file resolution via folder_paths,
#    ffmpeg lookup + hard error on decode failure, and a required
#    `mouth_masks` MASK input — per-frame lower-face masks from the
#    OF_MouthMask node (MotionField pack), aligned to the decoded video frames.
#  - musetalk/utils/blending.py: get_image pastes the lip-synced face crop
#    back through that mouth mask (mouth contour + lower jaw hull) instead
#    of the upstream face segmenter — an all-zero mask (frame had no face)
#    leaves the frame untouched. The segmenter module is deleted by
#    setup-musetalk.sh (nothing imports it after this patch).
#  - musetalk/utils/preprocessing.py: landmark+bbox detection runs on the
#    vendored Apache-2.0 DWPose ONNX pipeline (musetalk/utils/dwpose_onnx/,
#    from IDEA-Research/DWPose onnx branch — keeps its LICENSE + NOTICE)
#    instead of mmpose/mmcv (no py3.14 wheels). S3FD (research-licensed
#    s3fd.pth) is removed entirely: the fallback bbox is derived from the
#    same DWPose face keypoints. Low-confidence keypoints stay in the
#    68-slot layout as missing; when nose points 28-30 are missing the box
#    is built from the valid points; a run with no usable face in any frame
#    raises a clear error. BGR frames are converted to RGB before inference.
#  - torch.load(..., weights_only=False) + map_location fixes where the
#    upstream assumed CUDA/default safety semantics (unet, vae, whisper).
#
